# Domatar Project Context

Domatar is a distributed app platform: one Tomcat 10.1 / Jakarta EE 10 / Java 17
platform WAR (`domatar.war`) over MySQL 8, apps packaged as JARs under
`WEB-INF/apps/`. See `docs/spec/Domatar.md` for the umbrella design.

This folder is the **public** product tree. Phased `Update-*.txt` plans,
workshop dumps, and the two-provider sim compose live in the sibling
workspace root `internal`. Do not copy those files here.

## Local stack

Single node (`deploy/docker-compose.yml`):

- `tomcat` + `db` at http://localhost:8080/domatar/ (override with `TOMCAT_HOST_PORT`)
- WAR is the bind-mounted `platform/war/target/domatar.war`.

## Rebuild + redeploy

Always use `clean package` (not bare `package`). Incremental Maven builds can
leave Eclipse ECJ "Unresolved compilation problems" stubs in app JARs under
`WEB-INF/apps/`; AppLoader then fails to load apps (e.g. `domatar`, `appstore`)
and `/Setup` reports the app is not in AppRegistry.

```
mvn -q -pl <modules>,platform/war clean package -am -DskipTests
docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml up -d --force-recreate tomcat
docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml exec tomcat curl -s http://localhost:8080/domatar/Setup
```

After `--force-recreate`, curl `/Setup` — it republishes the provider PubKey
even when bootstrap is already done.

If Setup fails with `'domatar' app not yet loaded`, check Tomcat logs for
`Unresolved compilation problems` / AppLoader load errors and rebuild with
`clean package` before retrying.

## Working preferences

- If Docker wedges ("did not receive an exit event", OCI setns errors), STOP and
  ask the user to reboot Docker Desktop. Do not fight Docker.
- Do NOT commit unless the user explicitly asks.
- Never change the v1 actId/ownId math, existing identifiers, or host names.
- When behaviour changes, update the living spec under `docs/spec/` in the
  same change.
